    q: 'Is there a tax benefit on education loan interest for study abroad in India?',
    a: 'Yes. Under Section 80E of the Income Tax Act, interest paid on an education loan taken for higher studies, including study abroad, is deductible from taxable income with no upper limit on the amount, for up to eight consecutive years starting from the year repayment begins. This applies to the loan taken by the student or a parent for the student\'s education. It only covers the interest portion, not the principal, and only loans from an approved bank or notified financial institution qualify, so check this status with the lender before assuming the deduction applies.',
